From 0013-nouveau-pstate-calc-timeout Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Krzysztof Kowalski <krzysztof7kowalski@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0013/0013] clk: timeout waiting for pstate work

nvkm_pstate_calc() waits for the async pstate work with an unbounded
wait_event().  The work wedges when the PMU is dead (e.g. after a
failed D3hot->D0 transition on the MacBookPro11,3, where gt215_pmu_send
blocks on a PMU that never answers): the pstate writer then sleeps in D
state forever and no later pstate write can ever succeed (raport 77).

Bound the wait with a 2 s timeout; on expiry drop the waiting flag so
the next writer is not stuck behind a stale "in flight" marker and log
the failure.

Signed-off-by: Krzysztof Kowalski <krzysztof7kowalski@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/clk/base.c |   14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/clk/base.c	2026-08-27 16:39:49.554374919 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/clk/base.c	2026-08-27 16:39:52.393267428 +0200
@@ -351,8 +351,18 @@
 {
 	atomic_set(&clk->waiting, 1);
 	schedule_work(&clk->work);
-	if (wait)
-		wait_event(clk->wait, !atomic_read(&clk->waiting));
+	if (wait) {
+		if (!wait_event_timeout(clk->wait,
+					!atomic_read(&clk->waiting),
+					msecs_to_jiffies(2000))) {
+			/* pstate work wedged (e.g. PMU dead after a failed
+			 * D3hot->D0): drop the flag so the next writer is
+			 * not stuck forever.
+			 */
+			atomic_set(&clk->waiting, 0);
+			nvkm_error(&clk->subdev, "pstate work timed out\n");
+		}
+	}
 	return 0;
 }
 
